    "title": "What channel is Fab Five broadcast for Michigan vs Arizona in Final Four",
    "text": "Updated April 4, 2026, 6:12 p.m. ETIt doesn't get much bigger than this for Michigan basketball.The 1-seed Wolverines play 1-seed Arizona in the Final Four of the 2026 NCAA Tournament on Saturday, April 4, at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis. The game is scheduled for an 8:49 p.m. ET approximate tipoff and will be televised on TBS and TNT, with streaming available on Sling TV.But that's just for the traditional broadcast.At the same time, the Fab Five will be hosting an alternative broadcast on truTV.Watch the Fab Five Michigan vs Arizona broadcast on Sling TVThat means Michigan fans can watch Jalen Rose, Chris Webber, Juwan Howard, Jimmy King and Ray Jackson as they breakdown the Wolverines' game vs the Wildcats in real time with a spot in the national title game on the line.The special broadcast was announced by TNT Sports and CBS Sports on Thursday and will be co-hosted by Adam Lefkoe.Here's what you need to know and how to watch the Fab Five broadcast:How to watch Fab Five broadcast for Michigan vs Arizona in Final FourChannel: TruTV.Tipoff: Approximately 8:49 p.m. ET.Streaming: Sling TV, HBO Max.Michigan's famed Fab Five will be hosting a special alt-cast during the Michigan vs. Arizona showdown. To find the game, just flip to truTV after the Illinois vs. UConn game ends.How to stream Fab Five broadcast of Michigan vs Arizona in Final FourThere are a couple options if you don't have traditional cable but want to watch the Fab Five show. The game is being shown on HBO Max, but you can also find it on Sling TV, which carries truTV.Streaming: Sling TV, HBO Max.Tipoff: Approximately 8:49 p.m. ET.Watch the Final Four on Sling TVWhat time is Michigan vs Arizona in Final Four of March Madness?Time: Approximately 8:49 p.m. ET.Date: Saturday, April 4.Location: Lucas Oil Stadium, Indianapolis.Who was in the Fab Five at Michigan?Jalen RoseChris WebberJuwan HowardJimmy KingRay JacksonAndrew Birkle is an assistant sports editor for the Free Press. Contact him via email at abirkle@freepress.com.Our editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, however our editorial decisions remain independent. If you buy through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices and availability may change.",
